From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 20:15:25 +0200
Subject: net: lantiq: dma: take identity and configuration from the driver

The four packet DMA controllers of this SoC are described by one
compatible and were told apart by an aliases node, whose entry the
driver read back with of_alias_get_id(). Their fabric configuration -
arbitration, burst length, polling interval, descriptor placement,
prefetch, byte enables, byte order, and one software poll quota with no
register behind it - arrived as thirteen properties per node.

None of that describes anything a board can wire differently, and an
allocator index in an aliases node is not a way to name a device. Both
move into the driver: a table keyed by the register base carries the
controller identity and its configuration together, and the identity is
exported so that a driver holding a phandle to a controller can name a
channel on it.

The values are the ones the device tree carried, per controller and
unchanged, including the fields that reach no register because their
setter returns early on that controller. Keeping those makes the table a
transcription rather than an interpretation.

The compatible is spelled the way the binding does.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

